# Metric health and propagation handoff

Status: **Pre-Phase-005 consideration accepted. Phase 006 has not started.**

Preserve:

- successful load/run ≠ healthy produced table;
- available statistic ≠ useful metric;
- metric existence ≠ normative threshold;
- threshold authority ≠ metric statistical meaning;
- Baseline range ≠ normative Expectation;
- local metric ≠ propagated metric ≠ derived reconciliation expectation;
- technical metric view ≠ separate business truth;
- upstream anomaly ≠ downstream failure;
- metric used for monitoring ≠ automatically safe for Execution Gate control;
- richer/expensive metric ≠ synchronous production-path requirement.

Future Phase 006 rules:

- Define purposeful per-asset metric profiles rather than calculating every possible statistic.
- Distinguish core, critical-field/business, transformation-specific, and diagnostic/on-demand metrics.
- Candidate metric families include load/output, volume, freshness, completeness, uniqueness/key integrity, validity/schema, selected distribution/quantile measures, relational/join/reconciliation measures, and business-semantic metrics.
- Metric applicability depends on semantic role, data type, grain, transformation, criticality, and consumer use.
- Avoid meaningless metrics such as quantiles for identifiers or universal column-level statistics without an identified failure mode/use.
- Threshold/margin semantics must distinguish hard Expectations, warning/failure bands, absolute/relative/asymmetric tolerances, Baseline-derived ranges, seasonality/cohorts, low-volume/sample-size behavior, and bounded exceptions.
- Metric propagation is selective and transformation-aware; do not recursively cascade every upstream statistic through Lineage.
- For transformations such as A+B→C, define valid reconciliation relationships from join/filter/aggregation/grain semantics rather than assuming arithmetic count conservation.
- Preserve local upstream evidence for Investigation even when it is not a downstream metric.
- Technical and business audiences may receive different authorized projections over the same underlying metric/Assessment truth.
- Preserve progressive availability: fast operational facts → core table health → enriched DQ/distribution health → diagnostic/RCA → post-ops.
- Do not force monitoring metrics into the production critical path unless an explicitly accepted high-consequence control requires them.

Phase boundaries:

- Phase 005 decides metric/Expectation/threshold authority and disclosure governance.
- Phase 006 defines metric and health semantics.
- Phase 007 refines Lineage-aware propagation/operational use.
- Phase 009 evaluates actual source support, cost, latency, and retention.
- Phase 010 selects computation/storage/fast-path architecture.

Do not begin Phase 006 without explicit user request.